codex
Trace found the boundary behavior precisely: pydantic-core emits declared fields first and extras second. Python-mode dict construction overwrites the first value; JSON-mode emits duplicate keys (for example `{"x":1,"x":2}`), whose consumers retain the extra value. The same defect appears inside nested models, and serialization aliases can collide too, so the fix needs to sanitize the model graph before delegating—not merely patch the returned top-level dict.
