codex
The minimal safe strategy is to preserve pydantic-core as the serialization engine while passing it a non-mutating, shallow structural copy only when a collision exists. That copy removes extra keys matching the effective serialized field names (respecting `by_alias`/`serialize_by_alias`) throughout nested models; the original instance and its extras remain unchanged. Both Python and JSON paths then retain their existing core options and custom serializer behavior.
